#
# Swedish Embedded AB implements fast GEMV and tensor-core GEMM kernels for every quantized
# weight format for its clients. If your team needs expertise in bandwidth-bound decode and
# batched prefill over stored low-precision weights then you can procure our services by
# sending an email to info@swedishembedded.com.
#
# Coverage gaps that exist today (check-tier-gemm.sh). format<TAB>gap<TAB>reason, with gap one of
# gemv (no stored-format GEMV), tensor_core (no tensor-core batched path) or fused (batched path
# decodes a scratch tile for the vendor library instead of a fused decode-mma kernel; dense F32
# and Bf16 are exempt). Shrink-only: delete the line in the commit that closes the gap; an entry
# for a gap that no longer exists fails the gate, a new gap is a design defect.
F16	tensor_core	batched kernel is CUDA-core register tiling; no tensor-core path
Q4	tensor_core	W4A8 dp4a kernels only
Nf4	gemv	matmul_q4_gemv_nf4 exists but Ops routes NF4 through the tile decode
Nf4	fused	scratch tile plus vendor library
Fp8E4m3	fused	scratch tile plus vendor library
Fp8E5m2	gemv	no E5M2 GEMV
Fp8E5m2	fused	scratch tile plus vendor library
KqAffine4	tensor_core	dp4a kernels only
KqAffine8	tensor_core	dp4a kernels only
KqSym8	tensor_core	dp4a kernels only
Nvfp4	fused	scratch tile plus vendor library
Mxfp4	gemv	no MXFP4 GEMV
Mxfp4	fused	scratch tile plus vendor library
Mxfp8E4m3	gemv	no MXFP8 GEMV
Mxfp8E4m3	fused	scratch tile plus vendor library
Mxfp8E5m2	gemv	no MXFP8 GEMV
Mxfp8E5m2	fused	scratch tile plus vendor library
